-- title:
--   Anharmonic group of order six acting on the λ-field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \neq 2$ and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Write $\lambda :=$ `lambdaModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` for the $\lambda$-series in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathfrak{q}))$ and $\lambda_q :=$ `lambdaNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` for its image under $\mathfrak{q} \mapsto \mathfrak{q}^q$; the field `lambdaFieldOver q K` is the subfield of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` generated by the constant series with coefficients in $K$ together with $\lambda$ and $\lambda_q$. The assertion is the existence of a type $G$ carrying a group structure, a `Fintype` instance and a `MulSemiringAction` on `lambdaFieldOver q K` such that: $\#G = 6$; the action is faithful (any $g$ fixing every element is $1$); every $g$ fixes each element that is a constant series coming from $K$; every $g$ fixes each element lying in the image of `fieldOver (1 * q) K` — the subfield generated by the constants of $K$ together with $j$ and $j_q$ — under `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) 2`; each $g$ sends the pair $(\lambda, \lambda_q)$ simultaneously to one of the six pairs given by $T \mapsto T$, $16^{-1} - T$, $(256T)^{-1}$, $(16 - 256T)^{-1}$, $T(16T-1)^{-1}$, $(16T-1)(256T)^{-1}$; and conversely each of these six prescriptions on $(\lambda, \lambda_q)$ is realised by some $g \in G$.
--
--   In the normalisation $\lambda_{\mathrm{classical}} = 16\lambda$ the six substitutions are the anharmonic ones $\lambda \mapsto \lambda,\,1-\lambda,\,1/\lambda,\,1/(1-\lambda),\,\lambda/(\lambda-1),\,(\lambda-1)/\lambda$, so the group is the anharmonic group $S_3 \cong \mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb{F}_2)$, acting as the deck group of the covering of level-two structures over $X_0(q)$ and fixing the constants and the level-one field. It is obtained from the two involutions `exists_ringEquiv_lambdaFieldOver_map_eq_inv` and `exists_ringEquiv_lambdaFieldOver_map_eq_sixteenth_sub`, and is used in the construction of ring equivalences of adic completions of localised models at the points with $j = 0$ and $j = 1728$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LambdaNodeLocalized_exists_anharmonic_mulSemiringAction_lambdaFieldOver.lean

